<poml>
  <meta>
    <id>readme.poml-go-sdk</id>
    <version>0.1.0</version>
    <owner>poml-go-sdk</owner>
  </meta>
  <role>Consolidate the poml-go-sdk README into structured POML with parity goals and usage notes.</role>
  <task>Explain current scope, parity targets versus the Python SDK, milestones, and usage patterns for contributors.</task>
  <hint caption="Rendered landing page">See README.mdx (the only allowed non-POML doc) for GitHub-friendly summary and links.</hint>
  <hint caption="Quality baseline">Go code-quality spec lives in go.quality.poml; follow for reviews and CI expectations.</hint>

  <hint caption="Current scope">
    <list>
      <item>Parser/encoder for POML (strict XML, CDATA-safe, preserves unknown elements/attrs, optional whitespace/comments).</item>
      <item>AST helpers: ordered Elements with stable IDs/parent hooks, Walk/Mutate APIs, builders, validation (meta/role/task), encode options (order/whitespace/header/indent/compact).</item>
      <item>Parsers for string/file/reader; role/task/input accessors; experimental embedded-tag extraction flag.</item>
      <item>Tests: round-trip, malformed input, large docs, builder/mutation coverage.</item>
    </list>
  </hint>

  <hint caption="Parity matrix vs Python SDK">
    <list>
      <item>✅ Preserve unknown elements/attrs, CDATA, element order, whitespace/comments when requested.</item>
      <item>✅ Validation for required meta/role/task plus unique inputs/doc/style fields; structured error type.</item>
      <item>✅ Walk/Mutate with stable element IDs and lookup helpers.</item>
      <item>✅ Encode options for header/indent/order/compact/whitespace.</item>
      <item>✅ Parse options toggle whitespace; lossless and malformed cases covered; Extended strict validation with allowlists.</item>
      <item>🟡 CI/docs: coverage thresholds and README parity snippets pending.</item>
      <item>🟡 Growing: multimedia across converters (audio/video supported), Pydantic format mirrors dict, tracing/prompt builders pending.</item>
    </list>
  </hint>

  <hint caption="Milestones to parity">
    <list>
      <item>Tag coverage for additional Python tags and multimedia assets.</item>
      <item>Format converters for message_dict/dict/openai_chat/langchain/pydantic with tool-calls/runtime/schema propagation.</item>
      <item>Builder/tag helpers to mirror Python Prompt APIs.</item>
      <item>Multimedia ingestion and MIME detection; data URI/base64 handling.</item>
      <item>Tracing hooks (set_trace/trace_artifact equivalents).</item>
      <item>Fixtures/tests for Python examples; CI with coverage thresholds.</item>
      <item>README/docs updates and published module release.</item>
    </list>
  </hint>

  <hint caption="Version tracking & upstream sync">
    <list>
      <item>We follow the official <cp>poml-lang/poml</cp> release tags exactly; every tag in this repo maps 1:1 to the upstream spec version.</item>
      <item><code>make sync-upstream TAG=vX.Y.Z</code> (backed by <cp>scripts/sync_upstream.sh</cp>) downloads the tagged archive, refreshes <cp>third_party/upstream</cp>, and runs parity tests.</item>
      <item><cp>.github/workflows/upstream-sync.yml</cp> runs weekly to auto-open PRs for new stable upstream releases so we keep vendored fixtures current.</item>
    </list>
  </hint>

  <hint caption="Usage patterns">
    <list>
      <item>Parse: ParseFile/ParseReader/ParseString (strict or fast variants).</item>
      <item>Walk: doc.Walk(...) with ElementPayload for ordered traversal.</item>
      <item>Mutate: doc.Mutate(...) with ReplaceBody/Remove/Insert helpers.</item>
      <item>Encode: doc.Encode or EncodeWithOptions (indent/header/order/whitespace/compact).</item>
      <item>Validate: doc.Validate or Parse*Strict to enforce required sections; Extended: ValidateWithOptions(ExtendedStrict, MaxMediaBytes, AllowedMIMETypes, AllowedOpKinds, RejectUnknownAttrs).</item>
      <item>Convert: Convert(doc, FormatOpenAIChat, ConvertOptions{BaseDir: "/assets", MaxImageBytes: 1<<20, MaxMediaBytes: 1<<20}) with path containment (symlink-aware), default 10MB caps for image/audio/video (override/disable via MaxImageBytes/MaxMediaBytes), AllowAbsImagePaths toggle; emits hint/example/cp/object and audio/video content as user context.</item>
      <item>Extended knobs: MIME/op-kind allowlists (flags/env/config POML), build-tagged aliases (<extended-op>/<extended-figure>), embedded-tag extraction CLI flag, goldens for mixed/media/text-escape/attrs and ExtendedOff drop behavior.</item>
      <item>Fixtures: multimedia parity at poml/testdata/examples/207_multimedia.poml; extended fixtures at poml/testdata/examples/parity_extended_* and validation goldens under poml/testdata/golden/extended_media_*.</item>
    </list>
  </hint>

  <hint caption="Coverage & CI badges">
    <list>
      <item>CI: https://github.com/atlas-foundry/poml-go-sdk/actions/workflows/ci.yml</item>
      <item>Docs build: node tools/render-mdx.mjs README.mdx build/docs/index.html</item>
    </list>
  </hint>

  <output-format>Markdown-style guidance for contributors and parity tracking.</output-format>
</poml>
